"📖 Today was one of those days in our Burger Drops story that we’re going to tell our kids about. New York City has always held a piece of our hearts - the hustle, the people, the pace, the food, the hospitality, the scale — all within an island. It’s no wonder some call it the “City of Dreams”. There is an undeniable rhythm here that inspires you to truly strive for bigger and better.🗽\n\n❤️ Thank you to @motzburger, Dee, Seth, Mauri and the entire team at @hamburger_america for hosting us. It was an honour to work alongside you today and witness such a stellar operation come together.\n\n🤝 We turned online connections into in-person conversations, connected with new friends and presented our food to an international audience — all because we took a leap of faith one day to open our little burger shop. It’s emotional to say the least and a complete full circle moment. 😌\n\n🌇 This stop on the Burger Tour will be hard to match, BUT we’re bringing it home to Toronto next week with the valiant return of @motzburger on Friday, October 2 for the Meet, Greet & Eat event then $6 Oklahoma Fried Onion Burgers at 116 Atlantic Ave. on Saturday, October 3. 🎉 We hope to see you there and continue celebrating 6 years of BD! 🫡 #bdtour2026 #burgerdrops"